  <script type="module" src="/landing%20page/landing.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="landing-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="landing-header">
      <div class="landing-wrap header-row">
        <a class="landing-wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Ergon — back to top"><span class="wordmark-name">ergon</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><small>ἔργον</small></a>
        <button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-controls="landing-nav" aria-expanded="false"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button>
        <nav id="landing-nav" class="landing-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#features">Features</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#scoring">Scoring</a><a href="#privacy">Privacy</a><a href="#help">Help</a>
        </nav>
        <div class="header-cta"><a class="landing-button landing-button-primary" href="/app">Open Ergon <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </header>
    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="landing-hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-image" data-image-frame>
          <img class="hero-photo" src="/static/img/hero.webp" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
          <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="hero-fallback" role="note">Local hero photograph pending · add <code>public/static/img/hero.webp</code></div>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-wrap hero-inner">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-hero-enter><span class="eyebrow-rule"></span>HACKATHON PS-29 <span class="eyebrow-dot">·</span> MEETING-TO-TASK DELEGATOR</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title" data-hero-enter><span>Meetings don't fail on decisions.</span><em>They fail on vague promises.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-description" data-hero-enter>Ergon turns meeting transcripts into reviewable commitments: it surfaces vague language, shows what's missing, suggests clearer SMART tasks, and helps your team follow through.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions" data-hero-enter><a class="landing-button landing-button-primary" href="/app">Open Ergon <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="landing-button landing-button-text" href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <p class="greek-line" data-hero-enter>ἔργον · Greek for work, deed, task</p>
          <div class="hero-footnote"><span>01 / THE PROMISE</span><span>From conversation to accountable work</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="problem-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="problem-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="landing-wrap">
          <div class="section-intro"><p class="section-kicker"><span>01</span> THE PROBLEM</p><h2 id="problem-title">A meeting can end<br />with nothing owned.</h2><p>Hour-long conversations can leave behind an unclear promise—and no shared next step.</p></div>
          <div class="problem-lines">
            <p><span class="problem-number">01</span><strong>Everyone nodded.</strong><span>Nothing happened.</span></p>
            <p><span class="problem-number">02</span><strong class="quoted-promise">“I'll look into it.”</strong><span>A promise without edges.</span></p>
            <p><span class="problem-number">03</span><strong>No owner.</strong><strong>No deadline.</strong><span>No ticket.</span></p>
          </div>
          <p class="problem-note">When ownership, timing, or a deliverable is left unsaid, teams are left to reconstruct the commitment after the call.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="workflow-section section-pad" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="workflow-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="landing-wrap">
          <div class="section-head-row"><div><p class="section-kicker"><span>02</span> THE WORKFLOW</p><h2 id="workflow-title">From messy transcript<br />to tracked task.</h2></div><p class="section-aside">Three deliberate steps. Suggestions stay suggestions until a person reviews and confirms them.</p></div>
          <ol class="workflow-steps">
            <li><span class="step-index">01</span><h3>Paste</h3><p>Bring meeting notes or a supported transcript export. Ergon reads the text for possible promises and concrete follow-up.</p><small>.txt · .vtt · .srt</small></li>
            <li><span class="step-index">02</span><h3>Review</h3><p>Inspect the quote, the clarity signals, the missing owner, deadline, or deliverable—and edit the suggested SMART task.</p><small>Evidence stays visible</small></li>
            <li><span class="step-index">03</span><h3>Accept</h3><p>Confirm only the work your team is ready to own. Confirmed tasks move to the Board and appear in the Dashboard.</p><small>Human confirmation required</small></li>
          </ol>
          <div class="workflow-bottom"><span class="workflow-line"></span><span>Review → clarify → confirm</span><span class="workflow-line"></span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="features-section section-pad" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
        <div class="landing-wrap">
          <div class="features-title-row" data-reveal><div><p class="section-kicker"><span>03</span> THE WORKSPACE</p><h2 id="features-title">One promise.<br />Three ways forward.</h2></div><p>Start with the source. Keep every decision reviewable, then carry confirmed work forward.</p></div>
          <article class="feature-row" aria-labelledby="review-title">
            <figure class="product-figure" data-reveal><div class="product-window" data-image-frame><img src="/static/img/shot-review.webp" alt="Ergon Review screen capture." loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div class="asset-fallback" role="note">Authentic Review screenshot not included yet · add <code>shot-review.webp</code> to <code>public/static/img/</code></div></div><figcaption><span class="mono-label">WORKSPACE CAPTURE</span><span>Review · empty-state image pending</span></figcaption></figure>
            <div class="feature-copy" data-reveal><p class="section-kicker"><span>03.1</span> REVIEW</p><h3 id="review-title">Find the promise<br />behind the words.</h3><p>Read the transcript beside the suggestions. Ergon distinguishes possible commitments from general discussion and points to the source wording behind each one.</p><ul><li>See the exact transcript evidence.</li><li>Spot missing owners, deadlines, and deliverables.</li><li>Edit suggested tasks and their details before confirming.</li></ul><p class="feature-callout">The score is inspectable. The commitment is still yours to confirm.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-row feature-row-reverse" aria-labelledby="board-title">
            <figure class="product-figure" data-reveal><div class="product-window" data-image-frame><img src="/static/img/shot-board.webp" alt="Ergon Task Board capture showing To Do, Doing, and Done columns." loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div class="asset-fallback" role="note">Authentic Board screenshot not included yet · add <code>shot-board.webp</code> to <code>public/static/img/</code></div></div><figcaption><span class="mono-label">WORKSPACE CAPTURE</span><span>Board · empty-state image pending</span></figcaption></figure>
            <div class="feature-copy" data-reveal><p class="section-kicker"><span>03.2</span> BOARD</p><h3 id="board-title">Turn commitments<br />into work.</h3><p>The Board keeps approved tasks together for the current browser session, with the details a teammate needs to act and a simple view of where the work stands.</p><ul><li>Move tasks across To Do, Doing, and Done.</li><li>Review owners, deadlines, and deliverables.</li><li>Update task details as plans become clearer.</li></ul><p class="feature-callout">External ticket creation is not connected in this frontend preview. Jira and Slack are future directions, not current integrations.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-row" aria-labelledby="dashboard-title">
            <figure class="product-figure" data-reveal><div class="product-window" data-image-frame><img src="/static/img/shot-dashboard.webp" alt="Ergon Dashboard capture showing Meeting Debt and current-session metrics." loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div class="asset-fallback" role="note">Authentic Dashboard screenshot not included yet · add <code>shot-dashboard.webp</code> to <code>public/static/img/</code></div></div><figcaption><span class="mono-label">WORKSPACE CAPTURE</span><span>Dashboard · empty-state image pending</span></figcaption></figure>
            <div class="feature-copy" data-reveal><p class="section-kicker"><span>03.3</span> DASHBOARD</p><h3 id="dashboard-title">Make Meeting<br />Debt visible.</h3><p>Meeting Debt is a workflow heuristic calculated from unresolved promises in the current review session—not a forecast or a performance metric.</p><ul><li>Count identified commitments and clarity bands.</li><li>Find open tasks without an owner or deadline.</li><li>See approved work move through its statuses.</li></ul><p class="feature-callout">This repository is a browser-only preview. It has no shared or durable task store.</p></div>
          </article>
          <p class="capture-note">The GitHub repository does not yet contain the five WebP image files referenced here. Labeled fallbacks are shown; no mock interface screenshots or sample metrics are presented as real captures.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="scoring-section section-pad" id="scoring" aria-labelledby="scoring-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="landing-wrap">
          <div class="section-head-row score-head"><div><p class="section-kicker"><span>04</span> THE CLARITY MODEL</p><h2 id="scoring-title">A transparent score,<br />not a black box.</h2></div><p class="section-aside">Four explicit rules estimate how much clarification a potential commitment needs. Each contributes a named number of vagueness points.</p></div>
          <div class="score-layout">
            <div class="score-rules" aria-label="Vagueness score components">
              <div class="score-rule"><span>Owner missing</span><div class="score-bar"><i style="width:100%"></i></div><b>+30</b></div>
              <div class="score-rule"><span>Deadline missing</span><div class="score-bar"><i style="width:100%"></i></div><b>+30</b></div>
              <div class="score-rule"><span>Deliverable missing</span><div class="score-bar"><i style="width:67%"></i></div><b>+20</b></div>
              <div class="score-rule"><span>Hedge words</span><div class="score-bar"><i style="width:67%"></i></div><b>+20</b></div>
              <div class="score-legend"><span><i class="state-dot state-clear"></i>0–15 <b>Clear</b></span><span><i class="state-dot state-fuzzy"></i>16–45 <b>Fuzzy</b></span><span><i class="state-dot state-vague"></i>46–100 <b>Vague</b></span></div>
              <p class="score-translation">These are the scoring bands used by the repository's current local rules preview. A score flags details to review; it does not prove that a firm commitment was made.</p>
            </div>
            <aside class="worked-example" aria-label="Illustrative score example"><p class="mono-label">ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLE</p><blockquote>“I'll look into it.”</blockquote><p class="example-context">With no owner, deadline, or deliverable supplied:</p><ul><li>Owner missing <b>+30</b></li><li>Deadline missing <b>+30</b></li><li>Deliverable missing <b>+20</b></li><li>Hedge words <b>+20</b></li></ul><div class="example-result"><span>Vagueness</span><strong>100 <small>/ 100</small></strong><em>Vague</em></div><p class="example-foot">Illustrative rule calculation. A specific owner, deadline, or deliverable can lower the score.</p></aside>
          </div>
          <p class="scoring-footnote">Every score should show the rule that contributed and the exact transcript quote that triggered it.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section section-pad" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="landing-wrap"><div class="section-head-row"><div><p class="section-kicker"><span>05</span> DATA &amp; PRIVACY</p><h2 id="privacy-title">Clear about what<br />happens to text.</h2></div><p class="section-aside">A factual account of this repository's frontend preview.</p></div>
          <div class="privacy-columns">
            <article><p class="mono-label">01 / ANALYSIS</p><h3>Local rules only</h3><p>This frontend preview runs a small rules-based analysis in the browser. It does not call an AI service or API. Transcript text stays in the current browser session; the example transcript is sample content.</p></article>
            <article><p class="mono-label">02 / REDACTION</p><h3>No built-in masking</h3><p>The current preview has no redaction control. Remove sensitive details yourself before entering a transcript, even though this version does not upload it to an analysis API.</p></article>
            <article><p class="mono-label">03 / STORAGE</p><h3>Session, not sync</h3><p>No account, shared team store, or durable task database is connected. Do not rely on the browser preview as a long-term record or an offline-first application.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="help-section section-pad" id="help" aria-labelledby="help-title" data-reveal><div class="landing-wrap help-grid"><div><p class="section-kicker"><span>06</span> HELP</p><h2 id="help-title">A few useful<br />details.</h2><p>Know what the current browser preview does before you bring a transcript in.</p><a class="landing-button landing-button-primary" href="/app">Open Ergon <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <div class="help-list"><details><summary>What can I upload? <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The current page accepts .txt, .vtt, and .srt transcript files, or pasted text. Speaker names help the local rules preview anchor possible commitments.</p></details><details><summary>Does Ergon create tasks automatically? <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Review the suggestions and approve only the work you are ready to own. Approved tasks move to the Board in the current browser session.</p></details><details><summary>Does this version use AI or sync teams? <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. This repository is a frontend-only preview. It uses local rules, has no AI/API integration, and does not sync team records.</p></details></div>
      </div></section>

      <section class="closing-band" aria-labelledby="closing-title" data-reveal data-image-frame>
        <img src="/static/img/band.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div class="closing-overlay"></div><div class="closing-fallback" role="note">Local closing photograph pending · add <code>public/static/img/band.webp</code></div>
        <div class="landing-wrap closing-content"><p class="section-kicker"><span>07</span> FOLLOW THROUGH</p><h2 id="closing-title">Fix the promise<br />before it gets forgotten.</h2><p>Try Ergon and turn unclear meeting commitments into work your team can review and track.</p><a class="landing-button landing-button-primary" href="/app">Open Ergon <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="landing-footer"><div class="landing-wrap footer-main"><div class="footer-brand"><a class="landing-wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Ergon — back to top"><span class="wordmark-name">ergon</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><small>ἔργον</small></a><p>Meeting-to-task clarity, from transcript to follow-through.</p><span class="mono-label">HACKATHON PS-29</span></div><nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href="#features">Features</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#scoring">Scoring</a><a href="#help">Help</a><a href="/app">Open Ergon <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav></div><div class="landing-wrap footer-bottom"><span>ἔργον · work, deed, task</span><span>Built for clearer follow-through.</span></div></footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
